  "title": "Kourovka problem 18.20 (main)",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Characters φ and ψ of a finite group G are said to be semiproportional if\nthey are not proportional and there is a normal subset M of G such that φ|M is\nproportional to ψ|M and φ|G\\M is proportional to ψ|G\\M .\n   Conjecture: If φ and ψ are semiproportional irreducible characters of a finite\ngroup, then φ(1) = ψ(1).                                        V. A. Belonogov",
